      "worked": "At $x=1$, the point is $(1,1)$ and the tangent gradient is $y'=2(x-2)=-2$. Thus\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=-2(x-1)\\\\y&=-2x+3.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe intercepts are $X=(\\tfrac32,0)$ and $Y=(0,3)$. Therefore\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Area of }\\triangle OXY&=\\frac12\\times\\frac32\\times3\\\\&=\\frac94\\text{ square units}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
